  "hints": [
    "Treat every smaller total as a reusable subproblem.",
    "For each value, try every square no larger than it and extend the best result for the remainder.",
    "Initialize best[x]=x using x copies of 1. Replace it with min(best[x-square]+1) over square roots.",
    "The table grows from 0 upward, so every remainder has already been solved when it is needed."
  ],
  "editorial": "Dynamic programming defines best[x] as the fewest squares summing to x. Every optimal representation ends with some square q², leaving an optimal representation of x-q². Trying every possible final square yields the minimum. The independent oracle uses the four-square theorem and a two-square search instead of the DP recurrence.",
